00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:28.730
Now, if you've heard the term class reductionism,
there's a very simple analogy to at least

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:33.659
give us an initial basic understanding of
critical race theory, although it's not nuanced

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:34.659
enough.

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:40.319
And I admit that class reductionists believe
that at some fundamental level, any division,

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:47.400
any problem, any conflict, any inequality
in society, in politics, in an economy, even

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:53.210
if it seems it might be caused by many things,
is actually about class, something that to

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:59.219
a class reduction is something that looks
like a racial issue to a class reductionist.

00:03:59.219 --> 00:04:03.060
It's really a problem caused by class differences.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:07.269
And the racial factors may just be confounding
or they may be coincidental or they may not

00:04:07.269 --> 00:04:08.269
even be relevant.

00:04:08.269 --> 00:04:15.019
So to make a very rough analogy, to give us
a start in understanding critical race theory,

00:04:15.019 --> 00:04:20.949
critical race theory would analogously argue
that what might seem like a class problem

00:04:20.949 --> 00:04:27.110
or an economic problem or a political problem,
that it is actually fundamentally a problem

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:34.199
of race and racism in the U.S. specifically,
it would be racism generally by white people

00:04:34.199 --> 00:04:37.759
against nonwhite people, in particular against
black Americans.

00:04:37.759 --> 00:04:40.310
Now, that's the most basic explanation.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:44.140
It's far more detailed as an area of academic
research now for thirty years.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:48.069
And really even more than that, the roots
of critical race theory are in the sixties

00:04:48.069 --> 00:04:54.520
and seventies, but without getting into a
more nuanced definition, would include the

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:58.930
idea of creating subgroups of humans, developing
law and systems that are in.

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:05.180
Apparently racist and designed to maintain
these inequalities between whites and nonwhites,

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:09.169
